{"title":"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(combinatorial_via_Burnside’s_lemma)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (combinatorial via Burnside’s lemma)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine, with proof, all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c5984d0003c1ca2df2e68841dd9e93ed6c2d27c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{n+1} \\sum_{i=0}^n \\binom{n}{i}^k\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"57\" />is an integer for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/File:2025_USAMO_PROBLEM_5_1.jpg\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/File:2025_USAMO_PROBLEM_5_1.jpg</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/File:2025_USAMO_PROBLEM_5_2.jpg\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/File:2025_USAMO_PROBLEM_5_2.jpg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28combinatorial_via_Burnside.E2.80.99s_lemma.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(combinatorial_via_Burnside’s_lemma)\">Solution 2 (combinatorial via Burnside’s lemma)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (combinatorial via Burnside’s lemma)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e8e7e1356c164f137700fce34b9b9e6be7de7ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[X=\\{(A_1,\\dots,A_k):A_j\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,n\\},\\;|A_1|=\\cdots=|A_k|\\}.\\]\" width=\"444\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Then  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/5/1b5320ab675322e2ddb530964680ae49e6681b4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|X|=\\sum_{i=0}^n\\binom{n}{i}^k.\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>The cyclic group <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/2/662cb562a38c0847a1336a05357159b301a09238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> acts on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/804b3e12953126314c7deb59c40568709da57cb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,\\dots,n+1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" /> by “add 1 mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />,” and hence diagonally on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>By Burnside’s lemma,  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c00ef50d11b08a92a6445d8a5d5f80616722f031.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|X/C_{n+1}|=\\frac1{n+1}\\sum_{g\\in C_{n+1}}|\\mathrm{Fix}(g)|.\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> has order <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/f/a4fc920441df411e82ead8f5f2b17ab129eebd2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\mid(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c4226e9b38bdd708dad4903760de08a2c2e10b4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{Fix}(g)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" /> consists of choosing each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6edb286660f22d694ff4152ede3c948864cbb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> as a union of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2eaa3bc74bc3e0f479e1fe7239751d6082a36018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)/d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> orbits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, so  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b7462f180f4a500b94c06a16afd7b20c193688.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|\\mathrm{Fix}(g)|=\\sum_{i=0}^n\\binom{d}{i}^k.\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>Thus  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc1e0b64dd41cc073276982d5792842e0c9e5645.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n+1)\\,|X/C_{n+1}|=\\sum_{d\\mid(n+1)}\\varphi\\Bigl(\\tfrac{n+1}d\\Bigr)\\, \\sum_{i=0}^n\\binom{d}{i}^k.\\]\" width=\"350\" height=\"59\" />\n</p><p>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb89ec2cbdeebb1d7ad70c4b39301933f697cb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> even  \n</p><p>We prove by induction on the divisor‐lattice of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> that for every proper divisor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/3/4d31373a93a2c340b8532e8f942a5d623a50d5c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d&lt;n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />,  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e466dd7f5d580c56400a581315ae709a82530710.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d\\mid\\sum_{i=0}^n\\binom{d}{i}^{2m}.\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>Then each term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c8337c150956328f65bc1fe029d95deeac39b8d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi\\bigl((n+1)/d\\bigr)\\sum_i\\binom{d}{i}^{2m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"193\" height=\"58\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c60cd49160cd57fdef6b1f8e0597379bc61ea06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi\\bigl((n+1)/d\\bigr)\\,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"117\" height=\"24\" />, and since  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb5b767ce26fa801ae162e476850b1da2abc868.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{d\\mid(n+1),\\,d&lt;n+1}\\varphi\\Bigl(\\tfrac{n+1}d\\Bigr)\\,d =(n+1)-\\varphi(1)\\cdot1 =n+1-1,\\]\" width=\"434\" height=\"45\" />\nthe entire sum on the right is congruent modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> to  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f06495c1c71cd16a73a079b7c59c7b2070190df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\varphi(1)\\sum_{i=0}^n\\binom{n+1}{i}^{2m} =1\\cdot\\sum_{i=0}^n\\binom{n+1}{i}^{2m}.\\]\" width=\"324\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>But the left side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/0/1d092271f8ff0e55a66d725cb020c825bcb620a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)\\,|X/C_{n+1}|\\equiv0\\pmod{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"273\" height=\"20\" />, so  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242e5008a0a312925a9ac770187c62bf9b1d90e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n+1\\;\\bigm\\vert\\;\\sum_{i=0}^n\\binom{n+1}{i}^{2m}.\\]\" width=\"189\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>A re‐index <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/3226f299f88220be781c7ae86226ad322a6dbbb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1\\mapsto n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> yields  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f350d68e09fd28661c2eec7b27e0cee044aed97.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n+1\\;\\bigm\\vert\\;\\sum_{i=0}^n\\binom{n}{i}^{2m},\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"57\" />\nhence  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19df7c30a8ab5cc013cebf2d8fe1fbff1cd77aed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_{2m}(n)=\\frac1{n+1}\\sum_{i=0}^n\\binom{n}{i}^{2m}\\in\\mathbb Z.\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> odd  \n</p><p>Take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.  Then  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72c064f9ab86ae7dd978eb0e1a469d39a9bdea1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_k(2)=\\frac{\\binom21^k+\\binom22^k+\\binom23^k}{3} =\\frac{1+2^k+1}{3} =\\frac{2+2^k}{3}.\\]\" width=\"399\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is odd then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f7e37d1712de5e3eb381880f924d0a9e269125c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k\\equiv2\\pmod3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"22\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88f5b023076491a80660b5cfe3ef6473b36126ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+2^k\\equiv4\\equiv1\\pmod3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"189\" height=\"22\" />, whence  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8afde7a7843cf426ce180a592d8bedea7b0a73f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_k(2)\\notin\\mathbb Z.\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Conclusion  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb6c10f4679d114eb49d0444ae5e81c6519d2d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_k(n)\\in\\mathbb Z\\text{ for all }n\\ge1\\iff k\\text{ even.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"287\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO\" title=\"2025 USAMO\">2025 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018033546\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 247/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7674/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.946      1 -total\n 56.45%    6.743      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 40.97%    4.894      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31351:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018033546 and revision id 274114. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}